post css a tool for transforming styles  with javascript plugins when you build a  website the css code you write is rarely  the code that you actually want to ship  to the browser the developer wants to  write code with modern features that  maximize productivity but end users want  fast minified code that supports legacy  browsers post css is a build tool that  makes everybody happy it can take a css  file and convert it to an abstract  syntax tree then provides an api where  plugins written in javascript can  produce a different output for example  by using the auto prefixer plugin you'll  never have to worry about writing vendor  prefixes on your styles ever again or  with the preset enb plugin you can write  modern css while post css will  automatically add the polyfills needed  to support your targeted browsers or you  might drop in a tool like style and to  detect issues before they break your ui  and there are tons of other useful  plugins in the ecosystem to try out and  if none of them meet your needs you can  always build your own you might use the  plugin api to find all the color  declarations in the code then write some  javascript to transform them to a  different format you probably already  use post css without even realizing it  as it generates more npm downloads than  typescript and webpack can bind it's  used under the hood by frameworks like  veed and next js to provide a  streamlined developer experience and  it's also used by some of the world's  most popular websites like wikipedia and  twitter now despite its name it also  handles pre-processing similar to  frameworks like sas less and stylus it  can be used in conjunction with existing  preprocessors or as an alternative to  them altogether if you want to write css  with nesting or mixins there are plugins  that can enable those features in your  code so it's like configuring your own  css preprocessor by including your  favorite features and avoiding the ones  that tend to lead to bad practices on  top of that it tends to produce much  faster build times to get started  install it into your project with npm  then create a post css config file  inside of it customize the array of  plugins that you want to use and finally  run it from the command line as part of  your build process to make your styles  production ready this has been post css  in 100 seconds if you want to see more  short videos like this hit the like  button and subscribe thanks for watching  and i will see you in the next one
 

